-- title:
--   Equal branch values above a supersingular node of X₀(q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Let $a \in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero $k$-point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2} = a$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume $f$ is integral over `NodeLocalized.modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A.toSubring red a (a ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series $g$ admitting two-variable polynomials $r,s$ over $A$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a, a^q)$ after reduction and $g \cdot s(j, j_q) = r(j, j_q)$. Assume further that $f$ and its image under the Fricke involution `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` both lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by constants from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ at the complement of the kernel of reduction, and that their images under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lie in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $k$ generated by $j$ and $j_1$. Then there is a single $c \in k$ such that the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` takes the value $c$ on the reduction of $f$ and the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k (a ^ q)` takes the value $c$ on the reduction of the Fricke transform of $f$; 'takes the value $c$' means the element lies in the place's valuation subring and its residue is the image of $c$ in the residue field.
--
--   This is the form in which the Deligne–Rapoport description of the supersingular fibre of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$ is used: above the node $(a, a^q)$ of the plane model at a supersingular $j$-invariant there is a single point of the curve, so the two branches, read through the identity and the Fricke involution, assign the same value to any function integral over the local ring of the node. It feeds the crossing and node-vanishing statements used in the level-lowering step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_pow_eq.lean

